 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize Chabad at Stony Brook, Inc. to file an application for\nexemption from real property taxes for a certain parcel of real property in\nthe town of Brookhaven, county of Suffolk",
    "basePrintNo": "S8125",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8125-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8125\n\nSPONSOR: FLANAGAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to authorize Chabad at Stony Brook, Inc. to\nfile an application for exemption from real property taxes for a certain\nparcel of real property in the town of Brookhaven, county of Suffolk\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill will authorize the town of Brookhaven to accept from Chabad at\nStony Brook, Inc. an application for retroactive real property tax\nexemption for the 2017-18 assessment roll.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 gives authorization to the Town of Brookhaven to accept an\napplication for exemption and section 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nDIFFERENCE BETWEEN ORIGINAL AND AMENDED VERSION (IF APPLICABLE):\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAs requested by Chabad at Stony Brook.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill 2018.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
